etm-powersync-plugins (1.15.2+etm17) trixie; urgency=medium

  * New package powersync-plugin-generic-energy: the nymea genericenergy
    plugin leaves the separate nymea-plugins-genericthings copy and joins
    this fork. Imported from upstream 1.15.2 unchanged, then the three ETM
    commits applied on top. It provides, replaces and conflicts with
    nymea-plugin-generic-energy, and replaces and conflicts with the old
    monolithic nymea-plugin-genericthings, as upstream does. The nine other
    generic-* plugins stay the nymea packages.
  * genericenergy: removing an impulse smart meter destroyed nothing - both
    branches of thingRemoved() tested the same thing class, so its timer
    kept running and writing to a removed thing. Upstream defect, to be
    proposed upstream.
  * genericenergy: smartMeterConsumer, smartMeterProducer, energyMeter and
    wallbox integrate currentPower into their energy counters every second,
    over real elapsed time. Counters are monotonic; the sign of the power
    picks the counter (negative = produced, per the nymea interface). An
    action writing a counter suspends the integration of that thing for
    15 min. impulseSmartMeter keeps its own per-impulse counting.
  * Supersedes powersync-plugin-generic-energy 1.14.2+etm3, built from the
    former copy.
  * Not deployed.

