etm-powersync-plugins (1.15.2+etm2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * openmeteo: implement Contract A. Every state now carries its regime in its
    name — forecast* for prediction, observed* for satellite observation. The ten
    states mandated by the nymea weather/daylightsensor interfaces keep their
    names; prefixing them would break interface conformance.
  * openmeteo: publish PV power derived from GTI, plus pre-integrated energy over
    rolling 3/6/12 h windows, rest of today and tomorrow. Scalars only, no time
    series in a nymea state.
  * openmeteo: fix silently broken satellite observation. The satellite endpoint
    ignores "current=" — HTTP 200, no error field, simply no current block — so
    the observed states were never set. Now uses hourly + past_days and takes the
    last non-null sample.
  * openmeteo: add satellite-observed GTI per plane, and ensemble weather spread
    computed on GTI rather than GHI (GHI understates the dispersion of the
    published quantity, in the optimistic direction).
  * openmeteo: poll each upstream product at its own rate — forecast 1 h,
    satellite 1 h, ensemble 3 h — instead of 15 min for all three.
  * openmeteo: add performanceRatio thing parameter, default 1.00.
  * Built against nymea 1.15.2.

